      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "At the end of 2017, <strong>425,876</strong> people in France were training under an apprenticeship contract. The number had hardly moved in years: 432,995 at the end of 2013.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "TOTAL"
            ],
            "upto": "2017",
            "mark": "2017"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "In September 2018 a new law, “for the freedom to choose one’s professional future”, changed how apprenticeship works. Any training organisation could now open an apprentice training centre, and centres were funded for each contract they signed. By the end of 2019 there were <strong>486,789</strong> apprentices, +14% in two years.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "TOTAL"
            ],
            "upto": "2019",
            "mark": "2019",
            "notes": [
              {
                "time": "2018",
                "label": "2018 reform"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "In July 2020, in the middle of the pandemic, the government added an exceptional hiring aid: up to €5,000 for an apprentice under 18 and €8,000 for an adult in the first year. Instead of collapsing, the count jumped to <strong>661,409</strong> at the end of 2020, +36% in a single year.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "TOTAL"
            ],
            "upto": "2020",
            "mark": "2020",
            "notes": [
              {
                "time": "2018",
                "label": "2018 reform"
              },
              {
                "time": "2020",
                "label": "Hiring aid"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The growth went on. At its peak, at the end of 2024, France had <strong>1,048,840</strong> apprentices: 2.5 times the 2017 level.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "TOTAL"
            ],
            "upto": "2024",
            "mark": "2024",
            "notes": [
              {
                "time": "2018",
                "label": "2018 reform"
              },
              {
                "time": "2020",
                "label": "Hiring aid"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Who are the new apprentices? Mostly students in higher education. Apprentices preparing a higher-education diploma (BTS, bachelor, master, engineering degree) went from 167,048 to <strong>634,017</strong>; those preparing a secondary-level diploma (CAP, vocational baccalaureate…) from 258,828 to 380,468. In 2025, 62% of apprentices were in higher education.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "SECONDARY",
              "HIGHER"
            ],
            "upto": "2025",
            "mark": "2025"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "At the end of 2025 the count fell for the first time in the series: <strong>1,014,485</strong>, −3% on a year earlier. The hiring aid had been cut, most recently in February 2025 to €5,000 for firms with fewer than 250 employees and €2,000 for larger ones. The latest monthly figure, for 2026-07, is 911,425, −3% on a year earlier.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "level",
            "series": [
              "TOTAL"
            ],
            "upto": "2025",
            "mark": "2025",
            "notes": [
              {
                "time": "2018",
                "label": "2018 reform"
              },
              {
                "time": "2020",
                "label": "Hiring aid"
              },
              {
                "time": "2025",
                "label": "Aid cut"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Nothing comparable happened in the other countries with long national series. Since 2017: Norway +23% (to 2025); Switzerland +1% (to 2025); England −6% (to 2024). France also counts higher-education apprentices, which most countries do not, so compare the direction, not the levels.",
          "chart": {
            "view": "index"
          }
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "DARES, apprentices under contract (POEM), on Apprentix",
