        {
          "text": "Cedefop’s database describes <strong>34 apprenticeship schemes</strong> in Europe, each coded on the same questions: where it came from, who the learner is, what contract they sign, what qualification they get. Each dot is one scheme.",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "grid",
            "on": null
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "<strong>17</strong> schemes are old: introduced before 2000, 16 of them from a craft tradition, like Germany’s, Austria’s or Denmark’s dual systems.",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "grid",
            "on": "old"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Another <strong>10</strong> were introduced after 2012, and 14 schemes in all grew out of school-based vocational education: schools adding long periods of work to their programmes.",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "grid",
            "on": "school_origin"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Sort the schemes by those answers and two families appear: <strong>18 employer-based</strong> apprenticeships, where the learner has the status of an apprentice, and <strong>14 school-based dual tracks</strong>. 2 fit neither: Professionalisation contract (France), Apprenticeship programmes (Portugal).",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "families",
            "on": null
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "In the school-based family the learner often stays a student: in 9 of 14 schemes, against 0 of 18 employer-based ones.",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "families",
            "on": "student"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "A training agreement can replace the contract in 9 of 14 school-based schemes, against 1 of 18 employer-based ones.",
          "chart": {
            "layout": "families",
            "on": "agreement"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "And only employer-based schemes lead to a qualification you can get <strong>only</strong> through apprenticeship: 11 of them, against 0 school-based ones. In the others, the same qualification can also be earned in a school-based programme.",
