        {
          "text": "So which family works better? Neither group of countries clearly does better: median employment of young people who recently finished vocational training is 80.3% where schemes are employer-based and 78.8% where they are school-based, while vocational education graduates' advantage over general-education graduates is 7.9 and 11.4 points respectively.",
